## Query hadamard+fp8 fusion — VALIDATED (correct + isolated win), PR-pending
`SGLANG_DSA_FUSE_HADAMARD_QUANT` (gfx950, head_dim==block_size==128, query-only):
`triton_hadamard_quant.fused_hadamard_act_quant` replaces two-pass
`act_quant(rotate_activation(q))` (hadamard writes bf16 -> act_quant reads it back),
removing one bf16 HBM round-trip of the indexer query/layer. Re-validated gfx950 GPU4:
- correctness: fp8 **98% bit-exact**, dequant **cos 0.99993**, scale maxrel 3e-3 (the
  2% diffs are 1-ULP from fp32-matmul hadamard vs the reference kernel). Faithful drop-in.
- isolated: **2.24x at prefill** (8192x32x128: 129->58us), ~1.15x decode (launch-bound).
Unlike the dead-ends above this is a STRUCTURAL memory-pass elimination, not a HW bet:
correctness-preserving, zero-risk, gated opt-in. e2e TTFT contribution is small (kernel
is a minor slice) but strictly >=0. SHIP IT (do not mis-file as a "marginal kernel hunt").

e2e A/B (canonical: `run_glm5_ab.sh` FEATURE_ENV + `e2e_glm5.sh` + `e2e_table.py`;
graphs-on, 8192/512, A=OFF GPUs0-3 / B=ON GPUs4-7, no eagle). Median TTFT off->on:
c4 1616->1596 (-1.2%), c8 2667->2628 (-1.5%), c16 4737->4652 (-1.8%), c32 8899->8771
(-1.4%), c64 17356->16943 (-2.4%); E2EL ~-1% across; ITL flat; throughput slightly up.
**Consistent small win, never a regression** (c2 -25% is single-stream noise, ignore).
Minor GPU-set-bias caveat (A on 0-3 vs B on 4-7). STATUS: validated, PR pending (open
upstream PR as gated opt-in tomorrow). Fusion code already on origin (phase1/phase2).

